      "description": "Transitional: with the `label` filter gone, an open PR whose head SHA still carries a failed (or, in a narrow race at merge time, still-running) `label` check run from the deleted labeler is now labelled pr/ci-failing (or stuck at pr/ci-pending) by the push-to-main recompute-all, until its next push gives it a new head SHA; before, the filter ignored that run, so a failed labeler run could have sat unnoticed under pr/ready. It fixes itself and errs toward a stricter label, not a false pr/ready; I could not confirm that any open PR has such a run (only PR 257 could be queried, and its `label` run passed).",
